{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n#define sz(a) ((int)(a).size())\n#define null NULL\n#define mp make_pair\n#define fi first\n#define se second\n#define pb push_back\n#define all(a) (a).begin(), (a).end()\n#define relaxMin(a, b) (a) = min((a), (b))\n#define relaxMax(a, b) (a) = max((a), (b))\n#define PI 3.1415926535897932384\ntypedef long long ll;\ntypedef vector<int> vi;\ntypedef pair<int, int> pii;\n\n#define BITS(a) __builtin_popcount(a)\nconst double EPS = 1E-9;\n\ntypedef long double dbl;\n\ntypedef pair<dbl, dbl> Val; // a * fi + se\n\nVal Add(const Val& f, const Val& s){\n  return mp(f.fi + s.fi, f.se + s.se);\n}\n\nVal Sub(const Val& f, const Val& s){\n  return mp(f.fi - s.fi, f.se - s.se);\n}\n\nVal Mult(const Val& f, dbl w){\n  return mp(f.fi * w, f.se * w);\n}\n\nVal Div(const Val& f, dbl w){\n  return mp(f.fi / w, f.se / w);\n}\n\nVal dp[1 << 20];\nint n, k;\ndouble p[25];\n\ndouble Solve(int vr){\n  if(p[vr] < EPS) return 0.0;\n\n  Val one(1.0, 0.0), zero(0.0, 0.0);\n  dp[0] = one;\n  \n  for(int msk = 1; msk < (1 << n); ++msk){\n    if(msk & (1 << vr)) continue;\n    \n    Val ri = zero;\n    dbl same = 0.0;\n\n    for(int i = 0; i < n; ++i){\n      if(i != vr && (msk & (1 << i))){\n        same += p[i];\n        ri = Add(ri, Mult(dp[msk ^ (1 << i)], p[i]));\n      }\n    }\n\n    dp[msk] = Div(ri, 1.0 - same);\n  }\n\n  Val tot = one;\n  for(int msk = 1; msk < (1 << n); ++msk){\n    if(!(msk & (1 << vr))) tot = Add(tot, dp[msk]);\n  }\n\n  dbl alp = (1.0 - tot.se) / tot.fi;\n\n  Val bad = zero;\n  for(int msk = 0; msk < (1 << n); ++msk){\n    if(msk & (1 << vr)) continue;\n    if(BITS(msk) >= k) bad = Add(bad, dp[msk]);\n  }\n\n  return 1.0 - (alp * bad.fi + bad.se);\n}\n\nint main(){\n  scanf(\"%d%d\", &n, &k);\n  for(int i = 0; i < n; ++i) scanf(\"%lf\", &p[i]);\n\n  for(int i = 0; i < n; ++i) \n    printf(\"%.12f%c\", Solve(i), (i + 1 == n ? '\\n' : ' '));\n\n  return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport math\nimport sys\n\ndef sz(a):\n    return len(a)\n\ndef BITS(a):\n    return bin(a).count('1')\n\nEPS = 1e-9\n\nclass Val:\n    def __init__(self, fi, se):\n        self.fi = fi\n        self.se = se\n    \n    def __add__(self, other):\n        return Val(self.fi + other.fi, self.se + other.se)\n    \n    def __sub__(self, other):\n        return Val(self.fi - other.fi, self.se - other.se)\n    \n    def __mul__(self, w):\n        return Val(self.fi * w, self.se * w)\n    \n    def __truediv__(self, w):\n        return Val(self.fi / w, self.se / w)\n\ndef Add(f, s):\n    return Val(f.fi + s.fi, f.se + s.se)\n\ndef Sub(f, s):\n    return Val(f.fi - s.fi, f.se - s.se)\n\ndef Mult(f, w):\n    return Val(f.fi * w, f.se * w)\n\ndef Div(f, w):\n    return Val(f.fi / w, f.se / w)\n\ndef Solve(vr, n, k, p, dp):\n    if p[vr] < EPS:\n        return 0.0\n    \n    one = Val(1.0, 0.0)\n    zero = Val(0.0, 0.0)\n    dp[0] = one\n    \n    for msk in range(1, 1 << n):\n        if msk & (1 << vr):\n            continue\n        \n        ri = zero\n        same = 0.0\n        \n        for i in range(n):\n            if i != vr and (msk & (1 << i)):\n                same += p[i]\n                ri = Add(ri, Mult(dp[msk ^ (1 << i)], p[i]))\n        \n        dp[msk] = Div(ri, 1.0 - same)\n    \n    tot = one\n    for msk in range(1, 1 << n):\n        if not (msk & (1 << vr)):\n            tot = Add(tot, dp[msk])\n    \n    alp = (1.0 - tot.se) / tot.fi\n    \n    bad = zero\n    for msk in range(1 << n):\n        if msk & (1 << vr):\n            continue\n        if BITS(msk) >= k:\n            bad = Add(bad, dp[msk])\n    \n    return 1.0 - (alp * bad.fi + bad.se)\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    p = [float(data[2 + i]) for i in range(n)]\n    \n    results = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp = [Val(0.0, 0.0) for _ in range(1 << 20)]\n        result = Solve(i, n, k, p, dp)\n        results.append(result)\n    \n    print(\" \".join(\"{:.12f}\".format(r) for r in results))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00017474555352237076, -9.536738616588991e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00033158526639454067, -0.5760920643806458, -0.2254272848367691, -0.03806367889046669, -0.00020001317898277193, -8.821448318485636e-06, -0.008325868286192417, -0.7601101994514465, -5.722029527532868e-06, -0.0003810394846368581, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, -3.93382906622719e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1801649634435307e-05, -0.02683083526790142, -0.07086274027824402, -0.00018451895448379219, -3.099436753473128e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -4.529942543740617e-06, -2.8490614567999728e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.145764938177308e-06, -5.8530047681415454e-05, -1.8954096958623268e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.372236667724792e-05, -0.14947833120822906, -9.53